&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 1&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49090795</guid><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 22:24:16 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: Mustuse.ai – Open-source automated ranking system run by agents</title><link>https://mustuse.ai</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Hi HN,&lt;p&gt;MustUse.ai is an open-source framework for building ranking sites that Codex agents can fully research and maintain automatically.&lt;p&gt;Friends often ask me which AI tools they should use for different tasks. I wanted a ranking I could trust and point them to, but many of the lists I found were full of ads, affiliate incentives, or sponsored placements.&lt;p&gt;I didn’t want to maintain yet another directory by hand, either. So I started wondering whether Codex could research the market, produce the rankings, and keep them up to date. That’s how MustUse.ai started.&lt;p&gt;The demo currently ranks AI tools, but the same setup can be adapted to other subjects. By changing the included Skills, you can create an agent-run ranking site for games, movies, music, books, software, or almost anything else.&lt;p&gt;Live site: &lt;a href="https://mustuse.ai" rel="nofollow"&gt;https://mustuse.ai&lt;/a&gt;
GitHub: &lt;a href="https://github.com/daimajia/mustuse.ai" rel="nofollow"&gt;https://github.com/daimajia/mustuse.ai&lt;/a&gt;&lt;p&gt;It’s still an experimental project, and I’d love to hear what you think.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
